{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/786314-favorite-demon-lore-evocations","id":786314,"title":"Favorite Demon Lore Evocations?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-14T16:06:30-08:00","id":786314,"title":"Favorite Demon Lore Evocations?","content":"Some Demon Evocations are useful, particularly at upper levels, but some are just fun regardless of their raw POWAH. The first dot of the Lore of Light is fun because it is reminiscent of the Light the Angels wield in Supernatural. Another long time favorite of mine is the first dot in Lore of Portals simply because it evokes the imagery of Karou in Neon Genesis: Evangelion where he simply glanced at the high tech security lock and the thing opened for him. What Lore Evocations are your favorites and why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T18:47:07-08:00","id":786413,"title":"","content":"Lore of Awakening because, fourth dot aside, I find each of the abilities useful and much in line with what I like doing, namely mending the pains of others. To be completely fair with the fourth dot, it could be fun to make someone's drawer charge at them whenever they enter the room for shits and giggles. Lore of Radiance is also cool for the whole 'divine deity' image it conjures up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T19:07:34-08:00","id":786425,"title":"","content":"Sounds good, though I meant individual evocations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T05:18:05-08:00","id":786654,"title":"","content":"Well the lot of the two above buuuuut I rather like Lore of Winds 4 and the capacity of creating air-walls anywhere you like, sounds like you could have a decent amount of fun with that. Scry is always useful from Lore of the Firmament (is it obvious the Scourges are my favorite House yet?) and Mouth of the Damned of the same Lore could be so potentially hilarious I would be all for investing simply for that reason alone. I've always been a fan of the notion of being to shapeshift around however you like, so more or less the entire Lore of Transfiguration is good fun, but back on the above I particularly like the Mark thing you can do in Lore of Radiance 4 which is basically &quot;set a term, place the mark and you effectively have a pledge.&quot;<br /> Finally I'm very interested in what it would look like if an Earthbound went all out and unleashed Lore of Chaos 5; Hell On Earth. The description sounds fun alone, I wonder how it would play in a proper chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T06:09:03-08:00","id":786670,"title":"","content":"Lore of Chaos seems more interesting for me in a crossover-like chronicle (not necessarily a crossover per se, but borrowing freely from other cosmologies to expand on Demon's, and see the Fallen seeking to later understand the whole of the Umbra).<br /> <br /> I'm also a fan of the Scourge and their lores. Nowadays I'm toying with the idea of using Lore of Awakening 4 at a bunch of skeletons at an university or something, and sing Spooky Scary Skeletons while doing so.<br /> <br /> Another amazing lore is the Lore of the Forge. Each level is an unequaled source of wonders to literally toy with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}